[sliver] The long strip at each tip is the flat bearing that meets the east receiver wall. The production crest is 0.90 mm wide over the entire spring span.
alternatives: Rounding off this bearing restores the narrow contact of the pointed trial. Widening it changes the fitted lead-in and retaining geometry.
